{"id": "section-body-12938", "title": "Mycetoma (Madura Foot)", "chapterId": "chapter-thirteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "SKIN DISEASES", "Fungal Skin Infections", "Mycetoma (Madura Foot)"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-12938", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Mycetoma (Madura Foot)", "runs": [{"text": "Mycetoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(Madura"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Foot)"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1368"}}, {"id": "body-12939", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Mycetoma is a chronic disease usually of the foot, but any part of the body can be affected. Infection is most probably acquired by traumatic inoculation of fungi (eumycetoma) or bacteria (actinomycetoma) into the subcutaneous tissue.", "runs": [{"text": "Mycetoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chronic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disease"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "foot,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "any"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "part"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "body"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "affected."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Infection"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "most"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "probably"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acquired by traumatic inoculation of fungi (eumycetoma) or bacteria (actinomycetoma) into the subcutaneous tissue."}]}, {"id": "body-12942", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation:", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation:"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-12943", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Painless firm subcutaneous mass", "runs": [{"te